# ── Option B: binary payload lives in GitHub Releases, NOT in git ──────────────
# The ~14 GB of tool archives/installers/wheels/extensions are published as
# release assets and rehydrated on a staging host by
# scripts/internal/fetch-artifacts.sh (DEVKIT_ARTIFACT_BASE) or an offline
# bundle from scripts/internal/build-bundle.sh. Only manifests (checksums),
# READMEs, and the small devkit-server binaries under bin/ are tracked here.
# These rules keep the payload from ever being re-committed into the submodule.
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.tar.xz
*.7z
*.whl
*.vsix
*.rpm
*.exe
*.msi
*.dll
*.part-*
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg

# Exception: the prebuilt devkit-server binaries + signing key that
# scripts/launch.sh executes directly must stay tracked.
!bin/
!bin/**
